WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.880
[REPORTER A]
Who was
the first to find him?

3
00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.780
[REPORTER B]
Could they please
answer a few questions for us?

4
00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:18.880
[REPORTER C]
Who's the culprit?
Are there any suspects?

5
00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:20.480
[REPORTER C]
Is there any
connection between this

6
00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:21.880
and the annihilation
of the Franky House?

7
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.100
[REPORTER A]
What's his condition?

8
00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.770
[REPORTER C]
Could you
give us a statement, please?!

9
00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.040
[CITIZEN A]
Hey, did you
hear about what happened

10
00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:27.880
at the Shipbuilding
island last night?

11
00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.910
[CITIZEN B]
Is it true?
Did he die?

12
00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:34.680
<b>Back Alley, Water Seven</b>

13
00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:31.710
Franky did this,
I just know it!

14
00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:36.500
Well, it might've
been those pirates

15
00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:39.300
who've been hangin' around
the shipyard the past few days.

16
00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:43.180
<b>The Roof of an Inn
Back Alley</b>

17
00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:48.100
So this is
where you've been.

18
00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:52.480
[SANJI]
We went through all
the trouble of renting a room,

19
00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:55.150
and no one's using it.

20
00:02:55.180 --> 00:03:00.940
I guess nobody
could sleep, huh?

21
00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:02.580
And where's Luffy?

22
00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.370
Over there.

23
00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:11.440
[CHOPPER]
So, where were you?

24
00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:15.550
I kept lookout around the rocky cape all
night.

25
00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:18.750
I wanted to be there in case Robin came
back.

26
00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:20.490
[CHOPPER]
Oh.

27
00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.660
She never said anything about leaving.

28
00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:28.660
I wonder where she went.

29
00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.370
[SANJI]
I think I'll try looking
around for her in town today.

30
00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.100
[CHOPPER]
Do you think
we're gonna find her?

31
00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:42.910
[SANJI]
Who knows?

32
00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:46.240
It's not like I have any place specific in
mind to check out.

33
00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:50.120
I just feel certain that she's still here
somewhere.

34
00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:52.460
If anything should happen,

35
00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:55.560
we should use this inn
as our meet-up point.

36
00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.530
I wanna help!
I'm gonna come, too!

37
00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:00.130
All right, then. Come on.

38
00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:01.300
Luffy!

39
00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:03.230
[SANJI]
Nami! What's wrong?

40
00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:04.690
[NAMI]
It's awful!

41
00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:08.070
The whole city's talking about it!

42
00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:10.030
Luffy, listen to me.

43
00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:13.280
Last night, something
terrible happened to Iceburg!

44
00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:17.740
[PAULIE]
What?! Iceburg
was shot in his home?!

45
00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:19.690
Stop screwing around!

46
00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.360
Is this some kind of joke?

47
00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:21.820
[LULU]
No joke.

48
00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:22.820
Is he alive?

49
00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.560
Who would do such a thing?
Everyone loves him!

50
00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.290
[LULU]
Yes, he's alive!
Calm down, Paulie!

51
00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:29.620
Listen to me for
a second, okay?

52
00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:32.230
He was discovered in his
room earlier this morning

53
00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:35.270
lying in a pool
of his own blood.

54
00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:37.300
Like I said: He's alive,

55
00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.650
but he's been unconscious
since he was found.

56
00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:43.490
You need to come to the main office
immediately!

57
00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.640
[KAKU]
Lulu! Where's Paulie?

58
00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.300
[LULU]
I just called him.
He'll be here soon.

59
00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:55.620
[KAKU]
Good. Reporters
are all over the place.

60
00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:58.600
It's mass hysteria out there.

61
00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.070
We're the ones who'd like
to know what happened.

62
00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:02.670
The office has
been torn apart,

63
00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.040
but there's no trace of
anything being stolen.

64
00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:09.040
No money, no valuables, nothing.

65
00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:11.680
If this wasn't a robbery
then the question is:

66
00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:14.720
Who would try to
kill Iceburg, and why?

67
00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:18.420
At any rate, we're in big trouble here.

68
00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:21.300
The city's in total panic.

69
00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.170
If anything should
happen to Iceburg,

70
00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:25.610
then it's not only the end
for the Galley-La Company,

71
00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:29.010
but the entire city
of Water Seven, as well.

72
00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:46.120
Doctor, please.
What is his condition?

73
00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:55.760
He was shot two
times in the front

74
00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.150
and another three from behind.

75
00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:01.440
I have no idea what happened
in that room last night

76
00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:04.510
but whatever it was,
it was brutal.

77
00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:05.720
[LULU]
According to forensics,

78
00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:08.520
there's no sign of the locks
being picked to his office

79
00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:11.020
or anywhere else
in the building.

80
00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:14.320
The incident occurred in a room no one
could have entered.

81
00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:17.600
The only thing out-of-place
they found was a mask

82
00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:20.130
you can buy just
about anywhere.

83
00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:27.480
Ice Pops from the shipyard?

84
00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:31.150
[NAMI]
Yes. I've heard
he's still unconscious.

85
00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:34.480
I thought everybody in this entire city
loved that guy.

86
00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:35.880
Why him?

87
00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:37.350
[SANJI]
Who're you talking about?

88
00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:40.300
He's the nice man that helped us out so
much yesterday.

89
00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:42.040
The president of the
shipbuilding company

90
00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:44.270
as well as the
mayor of Water Seven.

91
00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.610
[SANJI]
Hmm, sounds
like an important guy.

92
00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:49.140
[NAMI]
Yeah, it's pretty
much the worst thing

93
00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:51.440
that could've
happened to this town.

94
00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:52.980
I'll go check on him.

95
00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:55.310
Luffy! Wait up!
I'm coming, too!

96
00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:01.070
[SANJI]
On that note,
let's go look for Robin.

97
00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:02.570
Come on, Chopper.

98
00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:05.270
What about you?

99
00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:08.810
[ZORO]
Well, I think I'll
just wait a while.

100
00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.430
See how things turn out.

101
00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:16.790
[NEWSPAPER GUY A]
Extra!
Extra! Read all about it!

102
00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:20.530
Iceburg, our beloved mayor
and the hero of Water Seven,

103
00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:23.860
has fallen victim to
the hands of an assassin!

104
00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:25.630
"Mr. Iceburg Falls Victim to Assassin"

105
00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:26.570
This is an urgent news report covering the
incident!

106
00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:28.470
This is terrible!
Is Iceburg okay?

107
00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:31.340
How awful! Who would
do such a thing?

108
00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:33.190
Only pirates would
pull a vicious attack

109
00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:35.460
like that out of nowhere.
No doubt about it.

110
00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:37.660
I'd like to get my hands
on the ones that did it!

111
00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.960
There were a bunch
of pirates rampaging

112
00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.630
through Dock #1
just yesterday!

113
00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:44.200
[CITIZEN M]
You mean
the Mikazuki gang?

114
00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:45.900
I know it sounds crazy

115
00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:48.130
but I think the
government did this.

116
00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:50.420
What? What're
you saying?

117
00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:52.820
I'm talking about Corgy.

118
00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:55.150
Every time he comes
to talk with Iceburg,

119
00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:58.190
he gets rejected and leaves.

120
00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:00.930
I'm telling you, Franky did it!

121
00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:03.800
I don't really know what he's
trying to speak with him about

122
00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:06.230
but he must have
done this out of spite.

123
00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:08.370
I'd keep that theory to myself.

124
00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:10.010
If you openly blame
the World Government,

125
00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:13.210
it won't be taken lightly.

126
00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:15.320
[NEWSPAPER GUY A]
Is this diabolical criminal's

127
00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:17.290
goal to gain wealth or power?

128
00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.860
Who is this
nameless assassin

129
00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:21.030
that disappeared
without a trace?

130
00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.600
"Mr. Iceburg Falls Victim to Assassin"

131
00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:24.960
Who in the hell did this?

132
00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.500
I'm not gonna let
them get away with it!

133
00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.860
[ANNOUNCEMENT]
Thank you
for riding the sea-train.

134
00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:36.880
Next stop: The Blue
Station at Water Seven.

135
00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:39.210
Arriving momentarily.

136
00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:05.860
[REPORTER D]
Paulie!

137
00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:07.620
[REPORTER E]
A word, please!

138
00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:08.750
Can we get a comment about this incident?

139
00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:10.920
[REPORTER F]
What were you
told before you came here?

140
00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:12.220
Shut up, all of you.

141
00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:14.520
Get the hell outta my way.

142
00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:15.790
Tell us what explanation

143
00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:17.030
you were given
by your company!

144
00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:18.090
[REPORTER G]
Paulie, please! A comment?

145
00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:21.070
I don't have time for
this crap! Get outta here!

146
00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:22.300
[REPORTER D]
Are you aware of any incident

147
00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:24.440
that could cause someone
to target Iceburg's life?

148
00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:25.270
Anything at all!

149
00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:26.240
[REPORTER E]
There must be something!

150
00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:28.240
[REPORTER F]
Any altercations with pirates?

151
00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:30.080
Didn't you idiots hear me?

152
00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.550
Get outta here!

153
00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:37.120
So I guess the rumors are true.

154
00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:38.750
He was attacked.

155
00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:40.850
Yeah. So if we
go to the shipyard,

156
00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:43.220
it's likely we won't be
able to meet with him.

157
00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:45.660
[LUFFY]
Then let's
just go to his house.

158
00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:48.530
[NAMI]
I believe he lives
inside the main office.

159
00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:52.520
[FRANKY]
Kiwi, Mozu.

160
00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:57.860
Am I asleep? Is this a dream?

161
00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:59.460
This is no dream.

162
00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:01.300
Without a doubt,
this is the very spot

163
00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:03.370
where the
Franky House stood.

164
00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:05.540
But something
like this happening.

165
00:10:05.590 --> 00:10:07.620
Just seems so extreme.

166
00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:15.960
[FRANKY]
What the hell is going on?!

167
00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:29.000
[FRANKY]
Who would be stupid enough

168
00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:32.540
to do something like
this to my house?!

169
00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:37.480
Hold on. I know who.

170
00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:39.700
Damn you, Straw Hat Luffy!

171
00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:40.640
So this is your payback

172
00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:44.210
for us stealing your
200 million berries?

173
00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:47.980
How dare you treat my
faithful men this way!

174
00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:50.710
It's so heartless!

175
00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:53.880
[FRANKY]
Unforgivable!

176
00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:55.310
Franky! Bro!

177
00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:57.780
You came back!
Thank goodness!

178
00:10:57.810 --> 00:10:59.550
[FRANKY]
You guys are all right?

179
00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:02.420
What a relief. Thank goodness.

180
00:11:04.820 --> 00:11:06.220
[ZAMBAI]
It was terrible!

181
00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:09.360
Those pirates are completely insane!

182
00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:09.930
Listen.

183
00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:10.730
We've been keeping track

184
00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:13.310
of what the
Straw Hats are up to.

185
00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:14.590
We know there's
no way you're gonna

186
00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:16.660
let them get away with this!

187
00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:18.650
Where are they now?

188
00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:21.480
[SCARFHEAD]
We saw
them going into an inn.

189
00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:22.550
[BEARDFACE]
After that,
they headed over

190
00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:24.720
to the shipbuilding island.

191
00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:26.120
It's Dock One.

192
00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:26.930
They were there yesterday.

193
00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:29.110
I bet that's where they're going.

194
00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:33.180
[FRANKY]
Is that so? All right then.

195
00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:35.340
Straw Hat Luffy.

196
00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:39.080
When I find you, I'm gonna rip you apart.

197
00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:45.350
<b>Shift Station</b>
<b>North of Water Seven</b>

198
00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:50.170
Whoa! Granny! Granny!

199
00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:53.040
The wind is blowing like crazy!

200
00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:59.520
[CHIMNEY]
Crazy wind!
Crazy Wind! Crazy Wind!

201
00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:02.720
[KOKORO]
Enough already!
Keep it down!

202
00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:10.030
The southern wind, huh?
Must be Karock.

203
00:12:11.690 --> 00:12:14.340
[KOKORO]
The waves
are getting rough, too.

204
00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:15.460
If this keeps up,

205
00:12:15.490 --> 00:12:19.690
the Sea Train won't
be able to run tonight.

206
00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:21.530
[KOKORO]
Chimney!
Gonbe! Get ready!

207
00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:22.860
We're going back to the island!

208
00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:24.930
Okay!

209
00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:34.210
Aqua Laguna is coming.

210
00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:44.020
[emergency siren blaring]

211
00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:45.150
[ANNOUNCEMENT]
Your attention, please!

212
00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.000
Your attention please!

213
00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:49.870
This is the Water Seven
Weather Forecasting Center.

214
00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:52.800
As of now, an Aqua Laguna
severe weather warning

215
00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:55.070
has just been issued
for the entire island.

216
00:12:55.110 --> 00:12:56.940
Its arrival time
is estimated to be

217
00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:59.410
sometime between
midnight and 12:30.

218
00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:01.750
[CITIZEN O]
Oh yeah,
I guess it is about that time.

219
00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:02.510
[CITIZEN P]
I've been preoccupied

220
00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.450
with what
happened to Iceburg.

221
00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:06.620
[CITIZEN Q]
Hey!
Aqua Laguna is coming!

222
00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:09.270
Make sure everybody knows about the
warning!

223
00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:11.890
[CITIZEN R]
All right,
no more work for today!

224
00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:13.060
What'd he say?

225
00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:17.030
Aqua Laguna?
Oh! Excuse me!

226
00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:19.460
What was that broadcast about just now?

227
00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:20.240
[CITIZEN S]
What do you mean?

228
00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:22.140
Everybody knows what... Oh!

229
00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:24.470
Wait, are you
visitor here? Sorry.

230
00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:26.870
You've come sightseeing
at a really bad time.

231
00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.450
Aqua Laguna is an annual storm.

232
00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:31.590
It's about to pass through here.

233
00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:32.860
[SANJI]
A storm, huh?

234
00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:33.890
A big one.

235
00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:36.560
You're gonna need to evacuate to higher
ground.

236
00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:39.360
This entire city will be underwater soon.

237
00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:42.070
Underwater? Really?

238
00:13:42.110 --> 00:13:43.010
[CITIZEN S]
Don't worry!

239
00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:44.750
It's not going to happen
right this second!

240
00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:45.620
According to the forecast,

241
00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:47.720
it'll arrive sometime
around midnight.

242
00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:49.660
The locals have gotten used to it.

243
00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:51.590
Annual, remember? See ya!

244
00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:53.060
[SANJI]
Later!

245
00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:55.460
[CHOPPER]
Hmm, the
whole town will be...

246
00:13:55.490 --> 00:13:57.700
Wait! It's gonna sink?!

247
00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:59.430
Yeah, apparently so.

248
00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:01.670
We need to find Robin
and quick. Come on.

249
00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:02.910
Right!

250
00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:04.180
Can't you tell us anything?

251
00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:05.490
Hey! Iceburg!

252
00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:07.230
[RANDOM MAN A]
What happened here?

253
00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:09.410
[RANDOM WOMAN A]
What's going on?

254
00:14:10.210 --> 00:14:12.520
We can't go that way.

255
00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:14.590
Man, we're never gonna
find out what's going on

256
00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:17.420
unless we find some
way to get to Ice Pops.

257
00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:18.620
Uhm, excuse me!

258
00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:20.800
Can you tell me where the entrance of the
main office is?

259
00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:22.440
Yeah, it's at Dock One.

260
00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:24.810
But I don't think you're gonna have any
luck getting in.

261
00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.010
With everything
that happened here,

262
00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:29.380
they're only allowing authorized
personnel to get through.

263
00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:31.680
You're not alone.
Everyone wants in!

264
00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:33.020
We're all so worried about him.

265
00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:35.480
I see. Thank you!

266
00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:41.560
[FRANKY]
Look at all those people!

267
00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:44.000
What's all the commotion about?

268
00:14:44.180 --> 00:14:47.780
Well. The bigger the audience
the better, I always say.

269
00:14:47.850 --> 00:14:55.890
♪ rhythmic drumbeating ♪

270
00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:57.690
No! Don't tell me!

271
00:14:57.760 --> 00:14:58.890
[CITIZEN X]
It's that rhythm!

272
00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:00.960
[CITIZEN Y]
What?! Why now?!

273
00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:01.830
[FRANKY]
Hey! Guys!

274
00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:04.800
Question: Did you
just say my name?

275
00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:06.970
No, we didn't!
Just go away!

276
00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:10.100
Where is he? Where's
that coming from?

277
00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:13.840
[CITIZEN BB]
I don't see him.
Wait! He's up there!

278
00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:17.350
[FRANKY]
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

279
00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:21.180
Come on, everybody,
no need-to-be-shy!

280
00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:22.650
Say my name!

281
00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:24.690
[CITIZEN DD]
We don't wanna! Get lost!

282
00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:25.520
[CITIZEN EE]
You're the one

283
00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:27.160
who attacked Iceburg,
aren't you?!

284
00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:29.230
[CITIZEN FF]
Yeah! He has to be!

285
00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:31.160
[CITIZEN GG]
Just leave!
Get the hell outta here!

286
00:15:31.220 --> 00:15:33.890
Hang that
good-for-nothing punk!

287
00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:38.000
[FRANKY]
What a
bunch of noisy flies!

288
00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:40.170
I'm Water Seven's
number 1 su-per-guy!

289
00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:42.200
The face of the underworld,
and you know why!

290
00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:44.580
I'm the man with the plan,
the power and fame.

291
00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:46.840
And people everywhere
call out my name!

292
00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:48.550
Wow!

293
00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:52.800
Franky!

294
00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:53.590
<b>Franky
Franky Family Boss
Dismantler and Bounty Hunter</b>

295
00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:04.480
Come out and show
yourself, Straw Hat!

296
00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:06.910
Stop being such a pansy!

297
00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:09.580
Get out here and fight me already!

298
00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:11.910
I dunno how that weirdo
figured out my name...

299
00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:13.820
I've never seen him before in my life!

300
00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.610
Didn't you hear what those people said?

301
00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:18.010
I think that guy might be Franky!

302
00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:19.810
Then we've found him.

303
00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:24.120
[thinking]
He's the one
who beat up Usopp!

304
00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:28.090
[FRANKY]
This money belongs
to us now. Understand?

305
00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:41.140
No! Give it back!

306
00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:44.670
Give it back!

307
00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:47.680
[LUFFY]
If it wasn't for him...

308
00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:48.940
Luffy.

309
00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:54.720
[LUFFY]
Hey! Bikini Guy!

310
00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:56.490
[NAMI]
Hold on a sec!

311
00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:00.540
Huh?

312
00:17:03.650 --> 00:17:06.250
That's me. I'm Straw Hat.

313
00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:08.600
[CITIZEN A]
There's
still no information?

314
00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:10.930
[CITIZEN B]
What's going on?!

315
00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:11.970
[KALIFA]
Everyone.

316
00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:16.830
So, what's the word?

317
00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:22.550
[KALIFA]
You may enter,

318
00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:24.680
but try to keep your
voices down, please.

319
00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:26.940
Then he... He's okay?

320
00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:30.610
His injuries are still
serious but Mr. Iceburg

321
00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:33.410
has finally
regained consciousness.

322
00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:36.490
That's great news!

323
00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:38.560
C'mon, let's see
how he's doing!

324
00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:42.800
[PAULIE]
You're okay!

325
00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:45.470
Mmwell, I've been
better, I suppose.

326
00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:47.730
All things considered,
you're pretty lucky!

327
00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:50.060
Anyway, you just focus on getting better.

328
00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:51.770
In the meantime,
you can count on us

329
00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:54.040
to take care of
the shipyard, okay?

330
00:17:54.080 --> 00:17:55.880
Yes, of course.

331
00:17:55.910 --> 00:17:57.610
Now, I need to talk
to you about the people

332
00:17:57.640 --> 00:17:59.610
who broke into my
room last night.

333
00:17:59.650 --> 00:18:00.680
Uh, yeah.

334
00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:03.020
Well, that's still under investigation,
I'm afraid.

335
00:18:03.050 --> 00:18:04.890
[ICEBURG]
No. I remember them.

336
00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:05.560
Huh?

337
00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:06.900
[gasps]

338
00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:11.170
There were two.

339
00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:13.880
One of them was a large man
who was wearing a mask.

340
00:18:16.730 --> 00:18:22.540
Tall, with long black hair.

341
00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:25.680
[ICEBURG]
I could never forget those eyes.

342
00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:27.800
It has to be her.

343
00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:34.710
<b>He regained consciousness</b>

344
00:18:36.610 --> 00:18:38.740
I can't believe
what I just heard.

345
00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:40.690
Mr. Iceburg's awake, everyone.

346
00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:43.630
It looks like our mayor's gonna be okay!

347
00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:44.300
[CITIZEN C]
Is that true?!

348
00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:45.030
[CITIZEN D]
All right!

349
00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:45.880
[CITIZEN E]
I was so worried!

350
00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:48.490
[CITIZEN F]
I knew
he'd make it!

351
00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:54.890
So you're Luffy, huh?

352
00:18:54.930 --> 00:18:57.830
Didn't expect you
to look so shrimpy.

353
00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.740
I got a bone to pick with you,
kid.

354
00:19:02.770 --> 00:19:04.840
It seems you and your
gang had a little party

355
00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.780
at my place
while I was gone.

356
00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:14.130
<b>Kiwi (Left) and Mozu (Right)
The Square Sisters
of the Franky Family</b>

357
00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:08.880
When I came home,
now, what did I see?

358
00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:09.980
My house was ripped to shreds

359
00:19:10.010 --> 00:19:11.580
and my gang
was on its knees,

360
00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:13.720
and it's all thanks to Luffy.

361
00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:15.890
I'll make this
as plain as can be...

362
00:19:15.930 --> 00:19:18.960
when you mess with my boys,
you mess with Franky.

363
00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:20.930
I'd hate to
be you right now

364
00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:22.900
cause I'm on one hell
of a roll this week,

365
00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:25.230
and ain't nobody
gonna stop me!

366
00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.930
Now you can cry if you like,

367
00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:29.070
but either way I'm gonna
pound you so hard

368
00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:32.470
even your own mother won't
recognize you when I'm done.

369
00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:33.640
[NAMI]
Shut up!

370
00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:34.840
Huh?

371
00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:38.640
You jerk! Give us our 200
million berries back already!

372
00:19:38.680 --> 00:19:39.980
You hear me?!

373
00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:41.080
Huh?

374
00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:43.610
You want your money back, you say?

375
00:19:43.650 --> 00:19:48.020
Well that's a damn shame, cause I'm afraid
I spent it all!

376
00:19:48.690 --> 00:19:51.300
You pirates are all a bunch of sore
losers!

377
00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:53.270
Don't act all high and
mighty when you probably

378
00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:55.270
just stole the money
from someone else!

379
00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:56.590
[LUFFY]
The money doesn't matter.

380
00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:58.870
Maybe not to you, but it does to me!

381
00:19:58.930 --> 00:20:01.370
All I care about now
is getting revenge.

382
00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:06.100
So money or no money, I'm gonna make you
pay!

383
00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:08.410
[FRANKY]
You're stealing
my lines, you bastard!

384
00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:10.180
Are you trying
to make me mad?!

385
00:20:10.210 --> 00:20:12.740
[LUFFY]
Whatever!
Just come down here and fight!

386
00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:16.250
Ah! Uh-oh!
Everybody get out of the way!

387
00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:18.600
[CITIZEN H]
Franky's
going on a rampage!

388
00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:20.350
[CITIZEN I]
Run away!

389
00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:29.040
Is he holding his breath
or something? Weird.

390
00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:47.760
[CROWD screams]

391
00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:57.760
He just spit fire!

392
00:20:57.800 --> 00:21:00.170
Yeah, I can see
that much but how?!

393
00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:04.740
Oh? You scared?
Having second thoughts?

394
00:21:04.810 --> 00:21:06.140
[NAMI]
Careful. If he can do that,

395
00:21:06.140 --> 00:21:07.740
he might have
devil fruit powers!

396
00:21:07.840 --> 00:21:09.940
Okay, but that doesn't really help!

397
00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:22.120
If that guy did
eat a devil fruit,

398
00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:25.710
he wouldn't just jump in the
water for no reason, would he?

399
00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:28.650
Maybe nobody told him that
if you try to swim, you die.

400
00:21:28.670 --> 00:21:29.600
That'd be pretty pathetic,

401
00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:31.060
but at least it would
save us the trouble

402
00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:32.930
of fighting that weirdo.

403
00:21:43.810 --> 00:21:47.820
Aaaaahhh!

404
00:21:47.850 --> 00:21:51.620
I guess he can swim!
Lucky he didn't drown, huh?

405
00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:56.160
I didn't eat no devil fruit!
You think I'm crazy?!

406
00:22:00.910 --> 00:22:03.480
Doesn't matter to me!

407
00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:04.410
Can't surprise me.

408
00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:07.010
I heard about that
little power of yours.

409
00:22:10.450 --> 00:22:12.850
[FRANKY]
Strong Right!

410
00:22:21.590 --> 00:22:22.630
What?

411
00:22:44.090 --> 00:22:45.840
Luffy!

412
00:22:48.300 --> 00:22:50.670
[NAMI]
Hey! Are you okay?!

413
00:22:58.010 --> 00:23:00.820
If you don't have devil fruit
powers, then what are you?!

414
00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:01.850
Huuuh?

415
00:23:01.890 --> 00:23:05.790
You poor saps don't
know anything, now do you?

416
00:23:05.830 --> 00:23:08.360
All right then, I'll humor you.

417
00:23:09.300 --> 00:23:12.840
I'm just a normal guy with some extra
parts.

418
00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:16.230
A cyborg, you might say.
[chuckles]

419
00:23:24.250 --> 00:23:26.130
One of the Straw Hats did this?

420
00:23:27.940 --> 00:23:29.910
Sure about that? Of all people.

421
00:23:29.940 --> 00:23:32.040
Yes. And my personal
investigation

422
00:23:32.080 --> 00:23:33.380
led to the same result.

423
00:23:33.410 --> 00:23:35.980
To make sure, I had Lucci
contact the government

424
00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:37.980
to confirm her
identity and bounty.

425
00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:39.450
Coo coo! Yes.

426
00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:41.380
They said she's a
notorious criminal,

427
00:23:41.420 --> 00:23:44.190
so it's no surprise that
she'd do something dastardly

428
00:23:44.300 --> 00:23:46.200
to our boss, coo coo!

429
00:23:53.110 --> 00:23:55.910
Then our next course
of action is crystal clear.

430
00:23:55.970 --> 00:23:59.070
We gotta find those rapscallions and show
them what's what.

431
00:23:59.110 --> 00:24:00.610
What in the hell
were they thinking?

432
00:24:00.640 --> 00:24:01.940
Don't tell me
they're pissed off

433
00:24:01.980 --> 00:24:03.510
'cause we wouldn't
fix their ship!

434
00:24:03.550 --> 00:24:04.620
[KAKU]
I wonder that myself.

435
00:24:04.650 --> 00:24:07.220
But regardless of what
their motivations might be,

436
00:24:07.260 --> 00:24:09.020
the bottom line is that
they're the culprits

437
00:24:09.060 --> 00:24:10.520
and they need to be dealt with.

438
00:24:10.560 --> 00:24:11.390
[PAULIE]
In other words,

439
00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:12.530
we should just capture
the Straw Hats

440
00:24:12.560 --> 00:24:15.030
and interrogate them ourselves
instead of wasting time

441
00:24:15.060 --> 00:24:16.860
trying to figure
this crap out.

442
00:24:16.900 --> 00:24:18.470
None of this
makes sense to me

443
00:24:18.500 --> 00:24:20.370
but anyone who
messes with Galley-La

444
00:24:20.400 --> 00:24:23.040
is gonna have
hell to pay.

445
00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:32.410
[TILESTONE]
Hey!

446
00:24:32.440 --> 00:24:33.970
There's trouble!

447
00:24:34.010 --> 00:24:36.910
Shut up Tilestone, you're
way the hell too loud!

448
00:24:36.940 --> 00:24:39.950
You fools! You're
just as loud as he is!

449
00:24:39.950 --> 00:24:45.080
<b>Tilestone
Joinery, Caulking, and Sailmaking Foreman
Dock One</b>

450
00:24:39.980 --> 00:24:42.350
Oh! I didn't know you were up

451
00:24:42.380 --> 00:24:45.380
already Mr.
Iceburg... that's great! Hahaha!

452
00:24:45.380 --> 00:24:45.980
[pow]

453
00:24:45.980 --> 00:24:47.750
[TILESTONE]
Ohh!

454
00:24:47.830 --> 00:24:48.960
He may be awake,

455
00:24:49.020 --> 00:24:50.660
but that doesn't mean you
should scream his ears off!

456
00:24:50.700 --> 00:24:52.740
Take it down a
notch or two, okay?

457
00:24:52.770 --> 00:24:56.740
I'm sorry! I can't
help it! I swear!

458
00:24:57.840 --> 00:25:00.180
Oh! I almost forgot!
I gotta tell you something!

459
00:25:00.210 --> 00:25:01.810
[PAULIE]
Fine, but stay outside.

460
00:25:01.890 --> 00:25:03.060
You can tell me from over there.

461
00:25:03.090 --> 00:25:05.030
We got trouble with
that Straw Hat guy!

462
00:25:05.060 --> 00:25:05.880
I dunno what happened,

463
00:25:05.880 --> 00:25:07.850
but he got in a
big fight with Franky

464
00:25:07.880 --> 00:25:10.020
and they're both
wrecking up the shipyard!

465
00:25:10.100 --> 00:25:13.740
If we don't stop 'em,
who knows what they'll do!

466
00:25:16.560 --> 00:25:17.860
Straw Hat again?

467
00:25:17.860 --> 00:25:20.560
Well, at least we know where to find him.

468
00:25:23.430 --> 00:25:24.660
He's got some nerve.

469
00:25:24.700 --> 00:25:27.970
I'll teach that punk to show his face on
our turf!

470
00:25:31.070 --> 00:25:33.640
Now you can finally have a bit of peace
and quiet.

471
00:25:33.640 --> 00:25:35.550
Let them take care of Straw Hat.

472
00:25:36.610 --> 00:25:38.680
I'll be watching over
you in the meantime,

473
00:25:38.710 --> 00:25:40.750
so there's no need to worry.

474
00:25:47.620 --> 00:25:51.920
Gum-Gum Pistol!

475
00:25:57.070 --> 00:25:59.240
[CITIZEN J]
Watch out!
It's coming down!

476
00:25:59.580 --> 00:26:01.280
[CITIZEN K]
They're trashing the ship!

477
00:26:01.300 --> 00:26:04.570
[CITIZEN L]
Stop it!
Go fight somewhere else!

478
00:26:10.410 --> 00:26:12.280
Luffy! Tear him to pieces,

479
00:26:12.310 --> 00:26:14.280
and then make him
put some pants on!

480
00:26:14.460 --> 00:26:15.760
Hey, Bro!

481
00:26:15.790 --> 00:26:18.760
You gotta put on a good show!

482
00:26:25.870 --> 00:26:28.110
You're a lot tougher
than I thought you'd be.

483
00:26:28.140 --> 00:26:30.880
But I'm still gonna beat you, Bikini Guy!

484
00:26:31.980 --> 00:26:33.380
If you say so!

485
00:26:33.410 --> 00:26:35.010
Though it's gonna
take a long ass time

486
00:26:35.050 --> 00:26:37.580
with those weenie
attacks of yours!

487
00:26:47.830 --> 00:26:50.400
[FRANKY]
Weapons Left!

488
00:26:54.830 --> 00:26:57.770
Gum-Gum Whip!

489
00:27:06.900 --> 00:27:09.950
I can't see... It seems
like they both got hit!

490
00:27:09.950 --> 00:27:11.950
No! Look who it is!

491
00:27:13.020 --> 00:27:15.020
Who just punched me?!

492
00:27:20.020 --> 00:27:21.160
This is too easy.

493
00:27:21.190 --> 00:27:22.730
If you knew what
was good for you,

494
00:27:22.780 --> 00:27:25.520
you woulda skipped
town a long time ago.

495
00:27:25.550 --> 00:27:33.530
You're in for it now!

496
00:27:33.560 --> 00:27:36.730
Galley-La? Great,
that's just what I need.

497
00:27:36.740 --> 00:27:39.480
All right, the guys from
Dock One finally made it!

498
00:27:39.530 --> 00:27:41.840
Lock those losers up and throw away the
key!

499
00:27:41.870 --> 00:27:43.070
Woooo!

500
00:27:43.100 --> 00:27:44.970
[CROWD cheers]

501
00:27:53.680 --> 00:27:54.580
[CITIZEN Q]
All right!

502
00:27:54.610 --> 00:27:56.880
The foremen'll take
care of these guys!

503
00:27:57.060 --> 00:27:57.860
[CITIZEN R]
That was close!

504
00:27:57.890 --> 00:27:58.800
If they didn't show up,

505
00:27:58.830 --> 00:28:01.230
the whole shipyard
was gonna get totaled!

506
00:28:01.260 --> 00:28:02.900
Wow, lucky break!

507
00:28:02.930 --> 00:28:05.640
Finally, someone can put a stop to this
nonsense!

508
00:28:05.670 --> 00:28:07.940
I bet they hate Franky too!

509
00:28:07.990 --> 00:28:10.060
[FRANKY]
I'd butt out
of this if I were you.

510
00:28:10.090 --> 00:28:12.130
Once these fists start
rockin' and rollin',

511
00:28:12.160 --> 00:28:15.300
they don't discriminate
between pirates and shipwrights.

512
00:28:15.330 --> 00:28:18.070
[KAKU]
And that goes for
other people's property, too!

513
00:28:18.100 --> 00:28:20.670
Surely you don't expect
us to stand here gobsmacked

514
00:28:20.700 --> 00:28:22.500
while you wreck
our entire shipyard.

515
00:28:22.500 --> 00:28:23.500
[TILESTONE]
Hhhhhgh!
I'm warning you, Franky,

516
00:28:24.910 --> 00:28:26.910
if you don't pay for
these repairs in berries,

517
00:28:26.940 --> 00:28:28.040
you'll pay in blood!

518
00:28:28.050 --> 00:28:30.620
[PAULIE]
All right Tilestone, calm down.

519
00:28:30.650 --> 00:28:33.020
We can take care of Franky some other
time.

520
00:28:33.050 --> 00:28:37.820
We've got more important business to deal
with right now.

521
00:28:37.850 --> 00:28:40.220
Yeah. I'm lookin'
at you, Straw Hat.

522
00:28:40.250 --> 00:28:42.120
You know exactly
what I'm talking about.

523
00:28:42.130 --> 00:28:44.000
I don't know if
you're brave or stupid,

524
00:28:44.040 --> 00:28:45.770
but either way, you're dead.

525
00:28:45.820 --> 00:28:47.020
Wait, what?

526
00:28:47.060 --> 00:28:50.990
We just came here 'cause we
heard the news about Ice Pops.

527
00:28:51.020 --> 00:28:52.630
Wasn't enough
to wreck my house

528
00:28:52.660 --> 00:28:54.030
and beat up my boys, huh?

529
00:28:54.060 --> 00:28:54.900
What's wrong?

530
00:28:54.930 --> 00:28:55.860
Don't feel like a
man unless you're

531
00:28:55.870 --> 00:28:57.770
pounding the crap out
of shipwrights, too?

532
00:28:57.810 --> 00:28:58.880
I know that
puberty can make you

533
00:28:58.910 --> 00:29:01.140
do some really
crazy stuff, but wow.

534
00:29:01.210 --> 00:29:02.820
I don't even know
what's going on,

535
00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:05.270
so stop making fun of me!

536
00:29:05.300 --> 00:29:09.240
Play innocent all you like.
I won't go easy on you!

537
00:29:09.270 --> 00:29:11.910
Rope Action Half Knot!

538
00:29:13.940 --> 00:29:16.650
I can't breathe. Can't breathe.

539
00:29:20.010 --> 00:29:23.920
Air Drive!

540
00:29:23.960 --> 00:29:25.330
Damn it, just, go away!

541
00:29:25.360 --> 00:29:28.020
I told you shipwrights to
stay out of this, didn't I?

542
00:29:28.020 --> 00:29:32.060
I'm the one who owes
this guy a beating, not you!

543
00:29:36.130 --> 00:29:37.060
Coo!

544
00:29:37.140 --> 00:29:39.480
Go Galley-La! Show 'em
what you're made of!

545
00:29:39.510 --> 00:29:40.310
There's no way
they can beat

546
00:29:40.340 --> 00:29:42.740
the top 5 shipwrights
in the city!

547
00:29:42.740 --> 00:29:45.940
What? Why are the shipwrights
fighting against us too?!

548
00:29:45.950 --> 00:29:47.850
Makes me itchy.

549
00:29:50.820 --> 00:29:51.960
[LUFFY]
What're you doing?!

550
00:29:51.990 --> 00:29:54.260
I don't have any reason to fight you guys!

551
00:29:54.290 --> 00:29:55.920
Just hold on!

552
00:30:00.260 --> 00:30:01.960
Would you look at that?

553
00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:04.130
He's got devil fruit powers.

554
00:30:14.740 --> 00:30:16.840
Hey stupid, are you even listening?

555
00:30:16.880 --> 00:30:20.810
How many times do
I have to tell you bozos?!

556
00:30:20.850 --> 00:30:22.850
For the last time...

557
00:30:24.770 --> 00:30:27.600
[FRANKY]
Straw Hat is mine, damn it!

558
00:30:32.330 --> 00:30:35.170
Hm?

559
00:30:35.200 --> 00:30:36.270
Sorry Franky,

560
00:30:36.270 --> 00:30:39.070
but we don't have time
for your shenanigans today!

561
00:30:39.100 --> 00:30:42.840
Get the hell outta my way,
you flying monkey!

562
00:30:42.860 --> 00:30:46.570
[TILESTONE]
You're the one
who's in the way, Franky!

563
00:30:48.370 --> 00:30:49.870
Oh yeeeah!

564
00:30:49.910 --> 00:30:51.210
[CITIZEN V]
That's our Tilestone!

565
00:30:51.240 --> 00:30:54.210
He's even stronger than usual today!

566
00:31:02.220 --> 00:31:08.160
Coo coo! Coo coolookoo!
Coo coo! Coo coo!

567
00:31:09.680 --> 00:31:12.930
Hey, stop it!

568
00:31:30.240 --> 00:31:32.310
Damn, you guys are strong.

569
00:31:32.350 --> 00:31:35.480
But I still don't know why we're fighting!

570
00:31:40.520 --> 00:31:42.390
[PAULIE]
Straw Hat,
I think we're the ones

571
00:31:42.420 --> 00:31:45.220
who deserve an
explanation here, not you.

572
00:31:46.960 --> 00:31:49.360
Someone broke into
Iceburg's house last night.

573
00:31:49.400 --> 00:31:50.360
Shot him twice in the front

574
00:31:50.400 --> 00:31:53.430
and three times in the
back before they left.

575
00:31:53.470 --> 00:31:55.270
They were from your crew!

576
00:31:55.300 --> 00:31:58.310
That can't be! None
of us would do that!

577
00:31:58.370 --> 00:32:01.200
[thinking]
I'm never
gonna settle this, am I?

578
00:32:23.830 --> 00:32:25.500
[thinking]
That was Nico Robin.

579
00:32:25.540 --> 00:32:28.580
There's not a single doubt in my mind.

580
00:32:28.610 --> 00:32:32.220
But was that masked man one of the Straw
Hats as well?

581
00:32:32.240 --> 00:32:35.570
And why did they attack me in the first
place?

582
00:32:35.610 --> 00:32:38.140
Surely it wasn't
about their ship.

583
00:32:38.190 --> 00:32:42.160
No. They must've been
aiming to steal something.

584
00:32:42.180 --> 00:32:43.860
But seeing as they
left empty handed,

585
00:32:43.860 --> 00:32:47.140
I have a good idea what
they were looking for.

586
00:32:47.170 --> 00:32:50.400
The question is if they're
working with the government

587
00:32:50.440 --> 00:32:53.140
or if they want
it for themselves.

588
00:32:53.170 --> 00:32:54.840
Straw Hat Luffy.

589
00:32:55.660 --> 00:32:58.240
[REPORTER A]
This just in!
Breaking news!

590
00:32:58.560 --> 00:33:00.890
Iceburg has already
identified the culprits

591
00:33:01.060 --> 00:33:02.600
from the break-in last night!

592
00:33:02.630 --> 00:33:04.300
[REPORTER B]
What?!
Is that true?!

593
00:33:04.330 --> 00:33:06.040
Spread the word
through the city

594
00:33:06.070 --> 00:33:07.600
and we'll capture
them ourselves!

595
00:33:07.640 --> 00:33:10.540
We can't let those criminals leave Water
7!

596
00:33:10.570 --> 00:33:12.080
[CITIZEN W]
Who did it?!

597
00:33:14.340 --> 00:33:15.240
[REPORTER A]
Show no mercy

598
00:33:15.280 --> 00:33:17.710
to the monsters who
attacked our mayor!

599
00:33:20.520 --> 00:33:22.190
[REPORTER A]
Capture the Straw Hat Pirates

600
00:33:22.220 --> 00:33:24.420
no matter what it takes!

601
00:33:26.940 --> 00:33:30.010
Iceburg was shot?
That's news to me.

602
00:33:34.250 --> 00:33:36.950
That can't be, we...

603
00:33:39.120 --> 00:33:40.560
No way!

604
00:33:40.590 --> 00:33:43.240
We didn't shoot Ice Pops...
That's just crazy!

605
00:33:43.240 --> 00:33:44.610
There were two people who broke

606
00:33:44.640 --> 00:33:46.580
into his room and attacked him.

607
00:33:46.610 --> 00:33:48.110
He may have been hurt
but that doesn't mean

608
00:33:48.140 --> 00:33:50.280
he didn't get a
good look at them first.

609
00:33:50.460 --> 00:33:53.970
One of them was a big guy with a mask on.

610
00:33:53.970 --> 00:33:57.180
The other was a tall woman with black
hair.

611
00:33:57.660 --> 00:33:59.620
Iceburg told us
he recognized her

612
00:33:59.660 --> 00:34:00.690
and the government confirmed

613
00:34:00.720 --> 00:34:03.960
that she's a
member of your crew.

614
00:34:04.070 --> 00:34:08.280
The Archaeologist, Nico Robin.

615
00:34:08.310 --> 00:34:09.910
You're lying.

616
00:34:14.660 --> 00:34:16.260
I won't ask you
why... maybe your crew

617
00:34:16.320 --> 00:34:19.890
came to Water Seven on a
mission to kill Iceburg.

618
00:34:19.920 --> 00:34:22.160
Or maybe you really did
want your ship repaired

619
00:34:22.190 --> 00:34:25.360
and attacked him on a whim
after we turned you down.

620
00:34:25.390 --> 00:34:29.260
I don't know how you
pirates think and I don't care.

621
00:34:29.300 --> 00:34:31.060
Point is, you tried
to kill my boss

622
00:34:31.100 --> 00:34:34.040
and now I'm gonna
have to take you down.

623
00:34:34.090 --> 00:34:35.960
[CITIZEN A]
So he's
one of the culprits?

624
00:34:35.990 --> 00:34:38.400
Tie him up Paulie,
don't let that pirate go!

625
00:34:38.430 --> 00:34:40.000
This is bad.

626
00:34:40.030 --> 00:34:44.070
So he got shot five times,
but Iceburg's still alive?

627
00:34:44.100 --> 00:34:45.670
Don't look so surprised.

628
00:34:45.760 --> 00:34:47.930
That guy's as tough as nails!

629
00:34:47.960 --> 00:34:51.070
But if they tried it once
then these scumbags

630
00:34:51.070 --> 00:34:54.040
might try to go after
Iceburg a second time, too.

631
00:34:54.050 --> 00:34:56.350
So we're gonna
settle this now.

632
00:35:00.120 --> 00:35:02.290
[KAKU]
"Dead or Alive."

633
00:35:02.290 --> 00:35:04.790
The World Government
doesn't care either way.

634
00:35:04.800 --> 00:35:07.710
This is what it means to have a bounty on
your head.

635
00:35:07.740 --> 00:35:09.180
Therefore, you can't complain.

636
00:35:09.210 --> 00:35:12.640
No matter how terrible
your fate may be.

637
00:35:12.680 --> 00:35:13.610
You've broken the law

638
00:35:13.700 --> 00:35:17.640
and now the law has
turned its back on you.

639
00:35:17.680 --> 00:35:19.910
[LUFFY]
That's right.

640
00:35:19.950 --> 00:35:22.920
We chose to live this way.

641
00:35:22.950 --> 00:35:26.220
We're all outlaws.
But I don't care.

642
00:35:26.250 --> 00:35:27.160
You're wrong!

643
00:35:27.190 --> 00:35:29.660
If you knew Robin
you wouldn't say that!

644
00:35:29.690 --> 00:35:31.830
So you take that back!

645
00:35:31.830 --> 00:35:33.030
Luffy.

646
00:35:33.060 --> 00:35:34.770
[LUFFY]
Let me talk to Ice Pops!

647
00:35:34.800 --> 00:35:36.240
This has to be a mistake!

648
00:35:36.270 --> 00:35:37.940
There's no way it was Robin!

649
00:35:37.960 --> 00:35:40.130
We'd be fools to let
you anywhere near him!

650
00:35:40.310 --> 00:35:43.510
Criminals have no
right to make demands!

651
00:35:43.540 --> 00:35:46.780
He's right!
Tie up the culprits!

652
00:35:46.820 --> 00:35:49.790
Those bastards can't get
away with shooting our hero!

653
00:35:49.820 --> 00:35:52.090
Send 'em to the gallows!

654
00:35:52.120 --> 00:35:55.160
Hey, wait! Just calm down!

655
00:35:55.240 --> 00:35:57.850
[CITIZEN F]
Hold on!

656
00:35:57.880 --> 00:35:59.150
You can't fool me, missy.

657
00:35:59.180 --> 00:36:01.180
I saw you with
that Straw Hat guy!

658
00:36:01.220 --> 00:36:03.950
I bet you're one of the
criminals, aren't ya?

659
00:36:03.950 --> 00:36:04.790
Really?!

660
00:36:04.820 --> 00:36:06.490
Yeah! She was
riding along with him

661
00:36:06.550 --> 00:36:08.720
on a Yagara when he got here!

662
00:36:08.750 --> 00:36:10.080
We've got you now!

663
00:36:10.120 --> 00:36:12.890
You're gonna get what you deserve!

664
00:36:12.920 --> 00:36:15.760
Stop it! Let me go!

665
00:36:15.790 --> 00:36:16.490
Nami!

666
00:36:16.660 --> 00:36:19.260
Word of this is gonna
spread like wildfire.

667
00:36:19.290 --> 00:36:22.900
There's no place to
run and no place to hide.

668
00:36:22.930 --> 00:36:24.400
It's the end of the road.

669
00:36:24.430 --> 00:36:26.630
You pirates are going down.

670
00:36:27.200 --> 00:36:29.400
[NEWSPAPER GUY A]
Extra! Extra! Read all about it!

671
00:36:29.440 --> 00:36:30.840
The Straw Hat Pirates
were the culprits

672
00:36:30.870 --> 00:36:33.640
in the attack
against Mr. Iceburg!

673
00:36:34.510 --> 00:36:36.610
The Water-Water
Newspaper will purchase

674
00:36:36.640 --> 00:36:41.110
any information related to their
current location or actions!

675
00:36:42.350 --> 00:36:44.090
We know that the
culprits are still here

676
00:36:44.120 --> 00:36:47.820
on the island, so be
sure to stay on the lookout.

677
00:36:47.860 --> 00:36:49.460
We must band
together to hunt down

678
00:36:49.490 --> 00:36:52.360
the Straw Hats and
send them to the Gallows!

679
00:36:52.390 --> 00:36:54.700
[TOWNSPEOPLE]
– Yeah!
– Yeah!
